title: 'grandpa: gossip commits to light clients in rotating groups'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    GRANDPA commit messages used to be gossiped to only 4 randomly picked light clients
    per round. With many light clients connected to a node, their finality lag grew
    linearly with the number of light clients.

    Light clients now take turns in groups of up to 100, in the order of their peer ids.
    Each light client gets a commit at least every `ceil(light_clients / 100)` rounds,
    and outbound bandwidth spent on light clients stays bounded by the group size.
    Gossip towards full nodes and authorities is unchanged.
crates:
- name: sc-consensus-grandpa
  bump: patch
